  "body": "## Associated User Story\n\n[P5-45: Fix bugs](https://pt-502.atlassian.net/browse/P5-45)\n\nAs an officer or member, I want event drafts to survive location-map problems, long email addresses to fit the home page, and public Help pages to provide a clear path back to login.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Event form values are preserved when the map loads or a location is chosen.\n\n- Sunny: An officer fills in the event name, description, start time, and end time, then loads the map or chooses a location. All entered values remain, the location coordinates update, and the event saves with those values.\n- Rainy: The map provider is blocked or fails to load, or geolocation permission is denied. The form retains the draft, explains the problem, and allows manual coordinates or a named location with both coordinates left blank. Partial or out-of-range coordinates are rejected. An event without a map pin cannot use location-based QR check-in until a pin is added.\n\n### Long email addresses fit the member home page without overlapping nearby content.\n\n- Sunny: A member with an email address longer than 50 characters opens the home page. The full address wraps within its statistic card, and badges, other statistics, and buttons remain readable.\n- Rainy: The address has no natural word breaks or the viewport is narrow. The address still stays inside the card, and the page does not gain horizontal scrolling.\n\n### Signed-out Help pages provide a visible Back to login link.\n\n- Sunny: A signed-out visitor follows Help from the login page and uses the top Back to login link to return.\n- Rainy: A signed-out visitor opens Help directly from a bookmark or on a phone. The link is still present and works without relying on browser history or a referrer.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Tests pass\n\nLocal validation of this branch:\n\n```text\nbundle exec rspec spec/\n555 examples, 0 failures, 1 pending\n\nnode --test spec/javascript/*.cjs\n13 tests passed, 0 failed\n```\n\nAdded JavaScript regression tests for delayed/blocked maps, reconnects during loading, manual coordinate validation, and denied geolocation. Updated Rails coverage for saving without a pin, preserving form values after validation errors, and direct public Help-to-login navigation.\n\n### Rubocop\n\n```text\nbundle exec rubocop\n161 files inspected, no offenses detected\n```\n\n[GitHub Actions for this branch](https://github.com/FA26-CSCE431-software-engineering/PT-502/actions?query=branch%3Ap5-45-ui-bug-fixes)\n\n### Manual checks and documentation\n\nVerified normal and blocked map loading with a filled draft, saved-location selection, and saving the event. Checked long-email containment at 1280, 375, and 320 pixels with no horizontal page overflow. Checked login-to-Help-to-login navigation and direct mobile Help access.\n\nUpdated the officer/member Help instructions and the event-form, event-check-in, and member-home screenshots.\n\nCI now installs Node.js 22 and runs all JavaScript regression tests; the README documents the command. No new application dependency or database migration is required.\n\n### Conflict resolution and integration validation\n\nMerged the updated `main` (through `420f769`) into this branch and combined the stylesheet and officer-guide changes. Preserved the existing event-import instructions, the map fallback guidance, and all original P5-45 commits and timestamps.\n\nThe member-table template matches the corrected version now on `main`, preserving filtering, sortable headings, member import, the admins table, and manager-only actions.\n\nValidation after integration: **555 RSpec examples, 0 failures, 1 existing pending example; 13 JavaScript tests passed; RuboCop inspected 161 files with no offenses.**\n\n## Section D: Deferred items / exclusions\n\n- Non-author code review and the human-only maintainability checks remain for the reviewer. GitHub CI results are available at the link above.\n- The RSpec pending example already existed before this change.\n- No new RuboCop exclusions were added.\n",
